description:
Demolition of Bollo, Maugham, Lawrence, Reade, Shaw, Hardy and Verne Courts, Blackmore and Kipling Towers, Working Men's Club, garages and storage units east side of Shaw Court and redevelopment as part of Phase 2 of the 15 year regeneration of the South Acton Neighbourhood to provide the following:

* 756 residential units, including provision of some units on southern part of Recreation Ground, with replacement open space to be located on site of part of existing All Saints Road; 
* mixed uses with approximate proportion of floorspace for each use as follows:
- 2490m2 Retail (Class A1);
- 625m2 Office (Class A2 & B1), Food & Drink (Class A3);
- 997 m2 Live/Work Units;
- 100m2 General Industry (Class B2);
- 1775m2 Community/Leisure (Class D1 and D2);
- replacement of the existing Community Club (Working Men's Club);
with an overall maximum floorspace of 5987 m2; with provision of some floorspace on site of existing allotments and relocation of allotments to land south of Verne Court, Vincent Road and to land occupied by storage to the south west of the Recreation Ground;
* Surface, garage and underground parking to provide a maximum of 442 spaces, resulting in total maximum of 617 spaces (including replacement/rearranged existing parking); and 
* Landscaping. 

Outline Application (for approval of means of access, with all other matters to be reserved) (Environmental Impact Assessment Planning Application) (Application for Deemed Consent by LB Ealing). (CONSULTATION FROM OTHER BOROUGH)
